{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedTraceGram","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WeightedTraceGram","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGramProduct","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SignProdComm"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.weightedTrace_card_eq_regTraceForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.weightedTrace_card_eq_regTraceForm","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L202-L213","doc":"**The regular trace is the `c_λ = d_λ` case.**\n\nSo `QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_pi_matrix_det` is the weight-`d` specialisation of\n`weightedGram_det`, not an independent result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_det_ne_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_det_ne_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L180-L200","doc":"**The Gram of a weighted trace is nondegenerate exactly when no weight vanishes.**\n\nThis is the equivalence that `QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.SchurElementCriterion` carries\nas a cited hypothesis. Instantiated at the canonical symmetrizing trace, where `c_λ = 1/s_λ`\nand `1/s ≠ 0 ↔ s ≠ 0` over a field, it reads: *the Gram of `τ` is nondegenerate iff every\nSchur element is nonzero* — [geckpfeiffer2000] Thm 7.2.6.\n\n**It is not yet an instance of that class**, and must not be made one: see the module\ndocstring for the two algebra-specific facts still missing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_det_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_det_explicit","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L163-L178","doc":"**The determinant with the sign evaluated**: `∏_λ (-1)^(d_λ(d_λ-1)/2) · c_λ^(d_λ²)`.\n\n`weightedGram_det` leaves the sign as the signature of the transpose involution, matching the\nstyle of `QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_pi_matrix_det`; `QOU.MathlibExt.sign_prodComm` evaluates\nit. The two are separated because the signature is an equation in `ℤˣ` while the determinant\nlives in `K`, so the substitution is a cast step rather than a rewrite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_det","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L137-L161","doc":"**The determinant of a weighted-trace Gram matrix.**\n\n`∏_λ ± c_λ^(d_λ²)`, the sign being the signature of the transpose involution on `J λ × J λ`,\nevaluated in closed form by `QOU.MathlibExt.sign_prodComm` as `(-1)^(d_λ(d_λ-1)/2)`.\n\nWith `c_λ = 1/s_λ` this is the determinant identity of [geckpfeiffer2000] Thm 7.2.6 for a\nsplit semisimple algebra; with `c_λ = d_λ` it is the regular-trace case already merged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_apply_same","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_apply_same","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L126-L135","doc":"**The diagonal block is the weight times the transpose permutation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_apply_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram_apply_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L117-L124","doc":"**Different blocks are orthogonal**: the product of matrix units from different factors is\nzero in every coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.weightedGram","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L111-L115","doc":"**The Gram matrix of a weighted trace**, in the matrix-unit basis of the product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.trace_single_mul_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.trace_single_mul_single","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L98-L109","doc":"**The matrix-unit product rule**: `tr(E_ab · E_a'b') = δ_{b,a'} δ_{a,b'}`.\n\nThe whole Gram computation is this one identity; it is why the Gram is a permutation matrix\nscaled by the weight, and hence why its determinant is a pure power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.blockUnit_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.blockUnit_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L94-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.blockUnit_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.blockUnit_self","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L89-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.blockUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.blockUnit","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**The matrix unit `E_ab` of block `i`, as an element of the product.**\n\nThe declared return type is load-bearing: written inline, `Pi.single i (Matrix.single a b 1)`\nelaborates against the WRONG family — Lean infers `ι → J _ → K` rather than the dependent\n`∀ j, Matrix (J j) (J j) K` and reports an application type mismatch. Naming it fixes the\nfamily once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.weightedTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.weightedTrace","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WeightedTraceGram.lean#L72-L77","doc":"**A character-weighted trace on a product of matrix algebras**: `Σ_i c i · tr(x i)`.\n\nEvery trace on a split semisimple algebra has this shape; the regular trace and the canonical\nsymmetrizing trace of [geckpfeiffer2000] differ only in `c`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}